#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 960.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125269} :activity/id #uuid "c9d087b0-e0c7-5257-8039-6b926add5c2f" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048781 :topic/id #uuid "be3a8d83-d961-5a49-82b6-e2c59f1bcd4b" :topic/math-academy-id 1933} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125269 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125724 :tutorial/content "Just like we can compute second derivatives of single-variable functions, we can also compute second derivatives of multivariable functions.\n\nFor example, consider the two-variable function\n\n$$\nf (x, y)= x y^2 + e^{xy}.\n$$\n\nIts two first-order partial derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & ={y}^{2}+y{e}^{xy}, \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =2xy+x{e}^{xy}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f_x(x,y)$ and $f_y(x,y)$ are themselves functions that are differentiable with respect to both $x$ and $y,$ we can compute the **second-order partial derivatives** as well. \n\n- The partial derivatives of $f_x(x,y)$ with respect to $x$ and $y,$ denoted $f_{xx}$ and $f_{xy}$ respectively, are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{x}(x,y))={y}^{2}{e}^{xy}, \\\\ {f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y))=2y+xy{e}^{xy}+{e}^{xy}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The partial derivatives of $f_y(x,y)$ with respect to $x$ and $y,$ denoted $f_{yx}$ and $f_{yy}$ respectively, are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y))=2y+xy{e}^{xy}+{e}^{xy}, \\\\ {f}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{y}(x,y))=2x+{x}^{2}{e}^{xy}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe partial derivatives $f_{xy}$ and $f_{yx}$ are called **mixed partial derivatives** because they involve taking the partial derivatives with respect to different variables, $x$ and $y.$\n\nThe following alternative notations are also widely used to represent second-order partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}}{∂{x}^{2}}(f) & =\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}={f}_{xx}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\frac{{∂}^{2}}{∂{y}^{2}}(f)=\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}={f}_{yy} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}}{∂y\\,∂x}(f) & =\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y\\,∂x}={f}_{xy}\\,\\frac{{∂}^{2}}{∂x\\,∂y}(f)=\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x\\,∂y}={f}_{yx}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** In our example, the two mixed partial derivatives were equal:\n\n$$\nf_{xy}(x,y) = 2y + xye^{xy} + e^{xy} = f_{yx}(x,y)\n$$\n\nLater, we will see that under rather mild conditions on $f,$ we almost always have that $f_{xy}=f_{yx}.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "feb54aa0-17fb-5468-8b99-14174a6bd059" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2397 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "0eaae658-c43c-5756-80c4-c4462162b555" :step/math-academy-id 10558 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125270}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125270 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124440 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124244 :question/id #uuid "0a8f5141-941d-5059-9d9f-bf9e5b09096f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3127"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ea31275-77bd-59c7-8e1d-96e2e4b252a4" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048707} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050902}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124935} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125185} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235546} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268915} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268916} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335782} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335784} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348377} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382138} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382358} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382365} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382372} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436905} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436907} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566270} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572115} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572145}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding Mixed Second-Order Partial Derivatives"} :step/id #uuid "4f4f64aa-ab4f-5abb-8d9c-ca2aa2790b64" :step/math-academy-id 10559 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125271}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125271 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124441 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124245 :question/id #uuid "e16f6686-dffb-554e-a50a-8760e818439f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3129"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "503a0bfe-7c69-5ad0-ad1d-aa8692dae673" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124932} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124946} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268918} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268919} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268920} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268921} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348378} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348384} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348391} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348392} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382379} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382386} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436904} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436908} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572162} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572178} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572193}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing Expressions Involving Second-Order Partial Derivatives"} :step/id #uuid "a25341f7-8d06-561b-9802-42d2f9c792e8" :step/math-academy-id 10563 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125272}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125272 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125725 :tutorial/content "We can also define other **higher order partial derivatives** such as $f_{xxy}, \\, f_{xxyy}, \\, f_{xyxy},$ etc. \n\nFor instance, the function $f(x,y,z)= z\\cos(xy)$ has the first-order partial derivative\n\n$$\nf_y(x,y,z) = -xz \\sin(xy)\n$$\n\nand the second-order partial derivative\n\n$$\nf_{yx}(x,y,z)= -x yz \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)} - z\\sin{\\left(x y \\right)}.\n$$\n\nIf we differentiate again, with respect to $x,$ then we get the **third-order partial derivative** $f_{yxx}\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yxx}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{yx}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-xyz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =-yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xyz(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot y)-z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\cdot y \\\\  & =x{y}^{2}z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-2yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn general, to compute a $n$th-order partial derivative, we need to compute a sequence of $n$ individual derivatives." :tutorial/id #uuid "e256986d-ca95-50b3-a16c-0f46005b5c66" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2398 :tutorial/title "Higher-Order Partial Derivatives for Functions of  More Than Two Variables"} :step/id #uuid "f8b4cf47-e81c-516c-8eef-7d544743362a" :step/math-academy-id 10566 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125273}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125273 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124442 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124246 :question/id #uuid "a41bfb06-4372-5124-b910-4b35f19d148b" :question/math-academy-id "e-3130"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83724b66-0f15-5b94-9576-76e9dfd56d38" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124939} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124948} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268922} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268923} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268924} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335787} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335788} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348393} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381062} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381069} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382131} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422010} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422011} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436906} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436909} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483391} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572140}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding Higher-Order Derivatives"} :step/id #uuid "25a77626-7a96-5d1b-b087-a01012cbeb91" :step/math-academy-id 10567}] :activity/title "Higher-Order Partial Derivatives" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186124726}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422014} :activity/id #uuid "59407835-7bfb-56b8-b3fd-56d3687982eb" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048781 :topic/id #uuid "be3a8d83-d961-5a49-82b6-e2c59f1bcd4b" :topic/math-academy-id 1933} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422012 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422011 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c70e303-c80e-51d2-8821-2af0cf8b3950" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421995} {:answer/id #uuid "92245356-2a0e-55cd-8484-17313be9c3ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422003} {:answer/id #uuid "992b5993-493b-561e-9033-5437b3de59e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422004} {:answer/id #uuid "ca872c1a-6f89-5f8b-8336-d7cb854e1bcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4x{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422005} {:answer/id #uuid "d1afdc0c-1cf1-54cf-9c95-d81dfb59dc49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422006}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422006} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a95cb7d-93f6-5084-ade9-1c85a3b6b1f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fdce2d33-30de-52e0-89c4-590147a8c4ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-80479" :question/problem "Calculate ${g}_{xxy}(x,y)$ given that $g(x,y)=({x}^{2}+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the first-order derivative ${g}_{x}(x,y):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(({x}^{2}+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({g}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find ${g}_{xxy}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xxy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({g}_{xx}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})) \\\\  & =4y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "25f65be6-b106-53d1-9640-27a18badcd80" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422015}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422013 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422010 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07b7ad2e-54cc-50e3-9ca3-0b8efd17be6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4y+{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421994} {:answer/id #uuid "1f109dc7-15d8-584f-8e2b-595762c1a061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4xy+y{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421996} {:answer/id #uuid "44455996-432d-5a3d-8b99-8ba088ea40bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2xy+{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421998} {:answer/id #uuid "5e886d04-bc8d-58c5-9141-d4629aa452fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x{y}^{2}+y{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421999} {:answer/id #uuid "e3c5be38-2517-52b4-89a2-e748dfb3f71f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y+x+{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422007}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421994} :answer-field/id #uuid "31dfaa29-640a-5223-927a-6d7e182b7cd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422009}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "11508c24-c4aa-589a-b2fa-c4b12396bfe7" :question/math-academy-id "q-65070" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}_{xyx}(x,y)$ given that $f(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+y{e}^{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}+y{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =2x\\cdot {y}^{2}+y\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =2x{y}^{2}+y{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{xy}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x{y}^{2}+y{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =2x\\cdot 2y+1\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =4xy+{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find ${f}_{xyx}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{xy}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{xy}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4xy+{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1\\cdot y+{e}^{x} \\\\  & =4y+{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "4932cd51-46e5-51d8-99f7-f0e3336e3476" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422012}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422014 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124932 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b1340c-9ea7-510e-a7fe-a5318d1aa165" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421993} {:answer/id #uuid "2ea483d9-4903-536f-a106-b11346fafb16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421997} {:answer/id #uuid "646a4289-2437-5a76-800d-038e82b06562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422000} {:answer/id #uuid "654452d8-a947-5e7b-b22c-8a13e2ef81d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422001} {:answer/id #uuid "6b0fbde1-6b7d-56c5-b32e-24ed9e9df6a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422002}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421997} :answer-field/id #uuid "f436de7c-3f9a-5c8c-8ef3-8a7a55ee418d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122192}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9fe7b82e-efd4-53ad-afa8-cb700e6400e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-35936" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{xy}(x,y)+{f}_{yx}(x,y)$ given that  ${f}_{x}(x,y)=2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}_{xy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find ${f}_{yx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y)+{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\  & =4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "73d31843-2db2-5471-8b39-85a8ef5439bb" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422016}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422015 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268920 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "573ca17f-8b55-50aa-b136-59bd043a6536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266921} {:answer/id #uuid "5df633bf-d9fe-5623-9aed-bd0cc78f2d1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266974} {:answer/id #uuid "5fc7ddd0-7d66-560f-b925-d71f0a4f1da7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}+\\pi )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266989} {:answer/id #uuid "75e2d132-79e6-565d-b0a0-3480a84f1042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -\\sqrt{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267184} {:answer/id #uuid "aa6cc2bf-6cc9-5989-82ab-f94ca56c41d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267685}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266974} :answer-field/id #uuid "0722938f-1bbb-5341-b742-6808aa83c68d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268418}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3aaf83dc-c135-54d5-b395-8dc2f637ad0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-132894" :question/problem "Find ${g}_{xx}(x,y)-{g}_{yy}(x,y)$ at $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ given that ${g}_{x}(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)$ and ${g}_{y}(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y).$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({g}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo find ${g}_{yy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({g}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we evaluate ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ and ${g}_{yy}(x,y)$ at $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\ {g}_{yy}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n{g}_{xx}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})-{g}_{yy}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "999e1519-06f2-527e-a6e9-193c3c031bfa"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422016 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124939 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9137d290-41b5-56f3-91a0-1bd21a361f51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122235} {:answer/id #uuid "9a8c61f9-4828-5963-94b5-9c4024267fa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122236} {:answer/id #uuid "fb781ced-0c22-5194-a9bf-5a48f6b0b287" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122237} {:answer/id #uuid "54475861-eeaf-5969-a8d8-c01e85facc65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122238} {:answer/id #uuid "74a0e08c-a99c-5a0d-80ac-df9b1bbcc42b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122239}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186122236} :answer-field/id #uuid "0485544a-7efe-5a7c-a375-d04fc25e6208" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122234}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ca6dfc54-54dd-5d46-99aa-e23ca5426a6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-35969" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}_{xyx}(x,y)$ given that $f(x,y)={x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) \\\\  & =2xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{xy}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy) \\\\  & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find ${f}_{xyx}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{xy}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{xy}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ed57f383-5736-5d28-bb66-05e9dcdf8f3a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422013}}] :activity/title "Higher-Order Partial Derivatives" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421992}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483451} :activity/id #uuid "5b774f06-abdb-5ce8-b0a4-4f02fda3281c" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048781 :topic/id #uuid "be3a8d83-d961-5a49-82b6-e2c59f1bcd4b" :topic/math-academy-id 1933} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483431 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268920 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "573ca17f-8b55-50aa-b136-59bd043a6536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266921} {:answer/id #uuid "5df633bf-d9fe-5623-9aed-bd0cc78f2d1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266974} {:answer/id #uuid "5fc7ddd0-7d66-560f-b925-d71f0a4f1da7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}+\\pi )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266989} {:answer/id #uuid "75e2d132-79e6-565d-b0a0-3480a84f1042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -\\sqrt{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267184} {:answer/id #uuid "aa6cc2bf-6cc9-5989-82ab-f94ca56c41d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267685}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266974} :answer-field/id #uuid "0722938f-1bbb-5341-b742-6808aa83c68d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268418}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3aaf83dc-c135-54d5-b395-8dc2f637ad0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-132894" :question/problem "Find ${g}_{xx}(x,y)-{g}_{yy}(x,y)$ at $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ given that ${g}_{x}(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)$ and ${g}_{y}(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y).$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({g}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo find ${g}_{yy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({g}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we evaluate ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ and ${g}_{yy}(x,y)$ at $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\ {g}_{yy}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n{g}_{xx}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})-{g}_{yy}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0156998a-6e16-5b9a-9f34-3fa9b3ed9afa" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483504}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483451 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483391 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0edad87c-2a7e-5ce2-948c-23ebc4486f11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482835} {:answer/id #uuid "87f3dc21-f9fe-515d-b7a6-aa328708748c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483051} {:answer/id #uuid "8bd1a042-f0e1-5280-a93f-79b975c4ee9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483058} {:answer/id #uuid "a5057d38-1225-50a0-b6ad-25ed31fa235e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483092} {:answer/id #uuid "ed0e24a1-111c-5e17-8f98-c82fe143a3a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483210}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483058} :answer-field/id #uuid "58cd874b-d401-5dae-a003-642f47b6d5e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483268}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a8c3fd0e-01dd-58d7-b5d0-e6ecb2b5f479" :question/math-academy-id "q-65054" :question/problem "Evaluate ${f}_{zyx}(1,1,-1)$ for $f(x,y,z)=xy\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y+z).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{z}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y+z)) \\\\  & =xy\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y+z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{xy}{x+y+z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{zy}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{z}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{zy}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{z}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{xy}{x+y+z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\cdot (x+y+z)-xy\\cdot (1)}{(x+y+z)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+xy+xz-xy}{(x+y+z)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+xz}{(x+y+z)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{zyx}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{zy}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{zyx}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{zy}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}+xz}{(x+y+z)^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x+z)\\cdot (x+y+z)^{2}-({x}^{2}+xz)\\cdot (2(x+y+z)\\cdot 1)}{(x+y+z)^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x+z)(x+y+z)-2({x}^{2}+xz)}{(x+y+z)^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate ${f}_{zyx}(x,y,z)$ at $(1,1,-1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{zyx}(1,1,-1) & =\\frac{(2(1)+(-1))(1+1+(-1))-2({1}^{2}+1(-1))}{(1+1+(-1))^{3}}=\\frac{(1)(1)-2(0)}{(1)^{3}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "345a4ba2-99a5-54c6-920b-943ebcfbdddc" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483455}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483455 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335788 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0548138d-e543-5a54-a872-c6505ae35f31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{4y}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333031} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd21545-2656-5f34-8899-9e63ce0f1a99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333573} {:answer/id #uuid "56f12986-c08d-5855-9c32-e38ca3128af3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333777} {:answer/id #uuid "7279d9a1-e1cd-5962-b045-74040fa8edd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334026} {:answer/id #uuid "810185ca-f52f-5e5b-a85b-df54ad11e6a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{4+y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334135}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333031} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7a6c17f-ff74-5dd2-941a-c73839c7e4a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335605}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ab0f3803-2840-52ec-8174-767389c2fcc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-65071" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}_{yxx}(x,y)$ given that $f(x,y)={y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{yx}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})) \\\\  & =2y\\cdot \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4y}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find ${f}_{yxx}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{yx}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yxx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{yx}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{4y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot x-4y\\cdot 1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4y}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3fdcb306-4c4d-55b0-afc4-b7f0ddec864f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483474}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483474 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382379 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28fd9f48-019d-5f27-baf0-6a1841493cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+{y}^{2})-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382381} {:answer/id #uuid "2ecd2278-324d-5173-a901-03897d9ade19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+{y}^{2})-x(y+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382382} {:answer/id #uuid "1f517a1e-8bfc-56fe-bed2-6c99b6f579a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+{y}^{2})-4{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382383} {:answer/id #uuid "fd42600b-5686-573f-98cb-1cd8e2a97d37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+{y}^{2})-(2y+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382384} {:answer/id #uuid "b86868bc-6931-5551-b2ee-dc760e6b939c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+{y}^{2})-2y(y+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382385}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382385} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a514deb-d87a-5e16-bf0c-b2bff11c7a40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382380}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b4318c10-0a8e-5140-827c-8a0c895809ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-80466" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{yx}(x,y)+{f}_{yy}(x,y)$ given that  ${f}_{y}(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+{y}^{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}_{yx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =y\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find ${f}_{yy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+{y}^{2})-2{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yx}(x,y)+{f}_{yy}(x,y) & =-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+{y}^{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+{y}^{2})-2{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+{y}^{2})-2y(y+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+{y}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7500e142-5145-59e0-8086-fdd6d710a0a6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483431}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483504 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268923 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00508df2-67fc-5789-9478-c3e2d42771e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266152} {:answer/id #uuid "44da4fc7-1df8-536a-a190-f8c23a3e32f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266758} {:answer/id #uuid "63a9b984-28e7-58d3-8128-0a6d4ca98f26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267021} {:answer/id #uuid "88f1885b-f866-5cf3-96ea-874e43e6a210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267363} {:answer/id #uuid "8ebfbd8f-e225-52f2-af81-73501dcd099d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267416}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266152} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f17d030-5507-55e9-8f15-4689404588ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268545}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "01b2f238-4be0-502a-a439-500d85cd72b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-132961" :question/problem "Evaluate ${f}_{xxz}(1,\\frac{1}{2},\\pi )$ for $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡xyz) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)\\cdot yz \\\\  & =yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{xx}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{x}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{x}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =yz\\cdot (-yz\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{xxz}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{xx}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xxz}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({f}_{xx}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(-{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}\\cdot (2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)+xy{z}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}z(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)+xyz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate ${f}_{xxz}(x,y,z)$ at $(1,\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xxz}(1,\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ) & =-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot (2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi )+1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi )) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ec92f449-cc5d-5eb7-8ed8-e8baf8365b8f"}] :activity/title "Higher-Order Partial Derivatives" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482804}]}
